alized instruction — early registration is encouraged!\n\n***\n\n## Pickleball Beginner Skills & Play (15+) at the Miles Nadal JCC\n\nHave you tried pickleball and want to feel more confident on the court? This **Beginner Skills & Play** program is the perfect next step!\n\nDesigned for players with **some familiarity** with pickleball, this small-group program helps you build a strong foundation through guided instruction, skill development, and beginner-friendly gameplay. Each session blends coaching, drills, and structured play so you can apply what you’re learning right away in a supportive, low-pressure environment.\n\n🏓 **What You’ll Work On:**\n\n* Review of basic rules, scoring, and court positioning\n* Developing proper technique for serves, returns, volleys, and rallies\n* Introductory doubles strategy and on-court decision-making\n* Applying skills through structured practice games\n* Individualized feedback and interactive Q&A with the instructor\n\n***\n\n📍 **Location:** Miles Nadal JCC — 750 Spadina Ave. (enter through Spadina doors)\n👥 **Format:** Small-group instruction led by an experienced, friendly coach\n🎾 **Equipment:** Paddles and balls are provided (or bring your own)\n\n***\n\n🧡 **Why Join?**\n\n* Build confidence and consistency in your game\n* Learn in a welcoming, beginner-friendly environment\n* Get comfortable playing real games, not just drills\n* A great bridge between Intro clinics and Drop-In play\n\n🔔 **New to pickleball?**\nIf you’ve never played before, we recommend starting with our **Intro to Pickleball Clinic**.\n\nWhether you’re looking to play recreationally, improve your skills, or prepare for more regular play, this program will help you feel confident stepping onto the court. Come learn, play, and have fun! 🏓","startDate":"2026-11-14T15:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Miles Nadal JCC","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"750 Spadina Ave - M5S 2J2, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Drop-in Recreation - Volleyball, Basketball & Pickleball","url":"https://www.meetup.com/downtown-miles-nadal-jcc-sports-and-recreation/"},"performer":"Drop-in Recreation - Volleyball, Basketball & Pickleball"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Pickleball Intermediate Skills & Play (15+): Nov 14-28","url":"https://www.meetup.com/downtown-miles-nadal-jcc-sports-and-recreation/events/316504798/","description":"📅 **Registration Required in Advance**\nRSVP’ing on Meetup does **not** reserve your spot.\n👉 **[Register here](https://app.amilia.com/store/en/miles-nadal-jcc/api/Activity/Detail?activityId=bVdgqNV)**\n☎️ Or call **416-924-6211 ext. 0**\nSpaces are limited to ensure personalized instruction — early registration is encouraged!\n\n***\n\n## 🎾 **Pickleball Intermediate Skills & Play (15+)** *at the Miles Nadal JCC*\n\nAlready comfortable with the basics of pickleball and ready to take the next step? **Intermediate Skills & Play** is designed for players who want to improve consistency, refine technique, and apply smarter strategy during real gameplay.\n\nThis small-group program blends **coaching, targeted drills, and structured play**, helping you transition confidently into intermediate-level play. Each session builds progressively, allowing you to practice new skills right away in guided game situations with personalized feedback from an experienced instructor.\n\n***\n\n🏓 **What You’ll Work On:**\n• Refining technique for serves, returns, volleys, and rallies\n• Improving consistency and shot selection during play\n• Developing introductory doubles strategy and court awareness\n• Applying skills through structured practice games and scenarios\n• Receiving individualized feedback plus interactive Q&A with the instructor\n\n***\n\n🎯 **Program Highlights:**\n• Progressive weekly skill development\n• Guided practice matches and scenario-based training\n• Strategy discussions to improve on-court decision-making\n• Supportive environment focused on growth and confidence\nWhether you’re aiming to strengthen your recreational play or prepare for more competitive games, this program gives you the tools and awareness to elevate your performance.\n\n***\n\n📍 **Location:** Miles Nadal JCC — 750 Spadina Ave. (enter through Spadina doors)\n👥 **Format:** Small-group instruction led by an experienced, friendly coach\n🎾 **Equipment:** Paddles and balls are provided (or bring your own)\n\n***\n\n🧡 **Why Join?**\n• Build confidence and consistency at the intermediate level\n• Learn through real gameplay — not just drills\n• Receive personalized coaching in a supportive setting\n• A strong bridge between Beginner programs and Drop-In play\n\n🔔 **New to pickleball?**\nIf you’ve never played before, we recommend starting with our **Intro to Pickleball Clinic**.\n\nIf you’re ready to challenge yourself, improve your decision-making, and feel more in control during games, this program is for you. Come play, learn, and level up! 🏓","startDate":"2026-11-14T15:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Miles Nadal JCC","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"750 Spadina Ave - M5S 2J2, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Drop-in Recreation - Volleyball, Basketball & Pickleball","url":"https://www.meetup.com/downtown-miles-nadal-jcc-sports-and-recreation/"},"performer":"Drop-in Recreation - Volleyball, Basketball & Pickleball"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"The Battle of Lundy's Lane (LECTURE ON THE GO)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/the-history-of-parkdale/events/315269045/","description":"**The Toronto History Walks Explorer Pass is available. Get it now for $125.00 for 1 year of unlimited tours, email**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n**for more information or for signing up!**\n\nWe have an amazing \"Lecture on the Go\" series for 2026-2027. New topics and fascinating stories abound! Join me, and uncover the world and keep active, warm and cool during the winter and summer months!\n\nI started this walking classroom when we were under that horrible cloud called Covid. This series was popular and helped people get back into society and life.\n\nThe \"Lecture on the Go\" Series is open to members who have purchased the YEARLY MEMBERSHIP PASS, it's free for those members. If you wish to attend a lecture and you are not a yearly pass member then the price **per** lecture is $20.00.\n\nThe Battle of Lundy’s Lane was one of the largest and bloodiest battles fought during the War of 1812. It took place on July 25, 1814, near Niagara Falls. American forces had crossed into Upper Canada (Ontario) and were pushing north along the Niagara Peninsula. British troops, Canadian militia, and Indigenous allies moved to stop them, and the two armies met near a small country lane known as Lundy’s Lane.\n\nThe fierce battle lasted well into the night, with soldiers often fighting in darkness, and confusion.\nOne of the most important points in the battle was a hill where British artillery had been placed. Both sides recognized its importance and launched repeated attacks. It was incredibly intense, with troops charging, and retreating, again and again. Officers on both sides were wounded, and casualties mounted. By the time the battle ended, neither army had achieved a clear victory, but the Americans eventually withdrew from the area, leaving the British in control of the field. It was a costly struggle, and thousands were killed or missing.\n\nToday, the Battle of Lundy’s Lane is remembered as a turning point in the Niagara campaign and one of the defining battles of the war. The battle demonstrated the determination of the Canadians who fought to defend this country.\n\nAlthough the war itself ended without major territorial changes, Lundy’s Lane became an important symbol of resilience. Visitors can still explore the historic battlefield in Niagara Falls and learn about the dramatic events that unfolded there more than two centuries ago, and made the country we call Canada. If you like history and Canadian history at that, or want to learn so much more then this lecture is for you.\n\nUpcoming topics in the 2026 series:\n\n\\*Philosophy 1: Great Minds of the Western World: Goethe to Kant! - (December 2026)\n\\*Philosophy 2: Great Minds of the Eastern\nWorld: Chuang Tzu to Dalai Lama - (December 2026)\nLegacy of Triangle: How a New York Factory Scandal changed North America - (January 2027)\n\nSo book your plans now!\n\nThis event is for all levels and walkers, there are a few steps here and there to navigate, but mostly on one level. This event in a **non-walking** event.\n\nThe lecture begins on the steps of **Old City Hall** at the northeast corner of Bay Street and Queen Street West, and\nhas a ticket price of $20.00 per person, but **free with the yearly membership pass**.\n\n**Please note: Please e-transfer the ticket amount when booking your space for this tour! You can e-transfer to the following email at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**","startDate":"2026-11-14T17:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Toronto Old City Hall","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"60 Queen St W, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto History Walks","url":"https://www.meetup.com/the-history-of-parkdale/"},"performer":"Toronto History Walks"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Bloor Street, Toronto. All of it. (19.6 km)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/hike-to-eat/events/316720017/","description":"**Attendance policy is enforced for this hike**. See below for details.\n\nBack by popular demand, we're doing a mega hike along Bloor Street in Toronto. We'll trace the entire Bloor subway line and beyond. See how the landscape densifies from golf courses to strip malls to parks to gentrified neighbourhoods as we approach the Don Valley. The restaurants along the way highlight the cultural diversity of Toronto from 5 continents.\n\nYou need to be in decent shape and have a voracious appetite to do the entire route. However, as with other hikes, you are free to join and leave at any point. Those who complete the entire route will be eligible to buy a commemorative T-shirt (expected price \\~$23).\n\nThere are several restaurants to choose from at the end of the hike: Japanese ramen, Mexican tortas, Egyptian koshari, and Brazilian steaks. Further on at Chester station are even more options: Iranian, Indonesian, and Greek grilled meats. We're not making reservations, so find a group of like-minded people and grab a table.\n\nFor reference, here's a [map of all our past hikes](https://www.google.com/maps/d/edit?mid=1_FpYriQNv5okUB-oiCODi56uiRDgPGI&usp=sharing). We've covered a large chunk of Toronto and neighbouring cities.\n\n**Highlights**\nSegment 1: Markland Wood\n\n1. Markland Wood Golf Club (depart 12:30pm)\n2. Mississauga-Toronto border / Start (or end) of Bloor Street\n3. Bloordale United Church\n4. Matt's Burger Lab\n5. Highway 427\n6. Stari Grad / Zayzoun / Frenchie’s Doughnuts (depart 1:45pm)\n\nSegment 2: The Kingsway\n\n1. Bonimi\n2. Kingsway Fish & Chips\n3. Old Mill\n4. Chebureky House / Momo Ghar / Janchenko's Bakery (depart 3:05pm)\n\nSegment 3: Bloor West Village\n\n1. The CakeSmith\n2. Former Runnymede Theatre\n3. Marvelous By Fred\n4. Ohana\n5. Andrea's Cookies\n6. Thai Nyyom\n7. 9 Mile Jamaican Cuisine / Momoheart / Chito's / Ruru Baked (depart 4:25pm)\n\nSegment 4: Bloorcourt Village\n\n1. Bakerbots Baking\n2. Komi Banh Mi Bar\n3. Nosso Talho\n4. Szechuan Noodle Bowl\n5. Ambassador Pizza\n6. Filosophy / Levant Pizza\n7. La Bella Managua / Lalibela / Vit Beo\n8. Christie Pits Park\n9. PAT Central\n10. Hodo Kwaja / Dessert Fox\n11. Pizzeria Fornace / JJIN Toast\n12. Eva's Original Chimneys / Cong Caphe (depart 5:45pm)\n\nSegment 5: Downtown\n\n1. Souper Hot Pot / Myeongdong Gyoza Kalguksu\n2. Trinity-St. Paul's United Church\n3. Woojoo Bunsik / Zaad / The Daily Dumpling Wonton Co\n4. University of Toronto\n5. Koerner Hall / Royal Ontario Museum\n6. Eataly\n7. One Bloor\n8. Yuzuki\n9. The Manufacturers Life Insurance Company / Rogers HQ\n10. Church of St. Peter and St. Simon\n11. Prince Edward Viaduct\n12. End (or start) of Bloor Street at Broadview Ave (arrive 6:55pm)\n\n**Neighbourhoods**\nMarkland Wood > Bloordale Gardens > Eatonville > Islington - City Centre West > The Kingsway > Bloor West Village > High Park North > Junction Triangle > Bloordale Village > Bloorcourt Village > Christie Pits > Koreatown > The Annex > Yorkville > Upper Jarvis > St. James Town > Playter Estates\n\n**Map**\n[https://www.google.com/maps/d/edit?mid=1ESqH0dQk3idaJYpGztKGE8UVoR5wFX8&usp=sharing](https://www.google.com/maps/d/edit?mid=1ESqH0dQk3idaJYpGztKGE8UVoR5wFX8&usp=sharing)\n\n**How it works**\nHike starts punctually. Late or can't join at the beginning? Meet us at scheduled checkpoints.\n\nWe'll browse many food places but won't linger long. Grab ready-made food, or see the route in advance, organize takeout, then pickup along the way. The end of the hike is the only time when we can enjoy a leisurely meal.\n\n**Attendance policy**\nPlease check in with an organizer when you arrive. 24 hours before the hike, we'll note down who is on the confirmed list. Those that don't show up will be marked as no-show. Repeat offenders will be banned. Please change your RSVP if you can no longer attend.\n\nIf you got off the waitlist less than 24 hours before the event, you won't be considered a no-show.","startDate":"2026-11-14T17:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"210 Markland Dr","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Etobicoke","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"210 Markland Dr, Etobicoke, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Hike to Eat","url":"https://www.meetup.com/hike-to-eat/"},"performer":"Hike to Eat"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"November Meetup: Theo of Golden by Allen Levi","url":"https://www.meetup.com/books-brunch-meetup/events/316638709/","description":"Book Description:\n\nOne spring morning, a stranger arrives in the small southern city of Golden. No one knows where he has come from…or why…\n\nHis name is Theo. And he asks a lot more questions than he answers.\n\nTheo visits the local coffeehouse, where ninety-two pencil portraits hang on the walls, portraits of the people of Golden done by a local artist. He begins purchasing them, one at a time, and putting them back in the hands of their “rightful owners.” With each exchange, a story is told, a friendship born, and a life altered.\n\nA story of giving and receiving, of seeing and being seen, Theo of Golden is a beautifully crafted novel about the power of creative generosity, the importance of wonder to a purposeful life, and the invisible threads of kindness that bind us to one another.","startDate":"2026-11-14T18:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-3-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"","addressRegion":"","addressCountry":""}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Books & Brunch Meetup","url":"https://www.meetup.com/books-brunch-meetup/"},"performer":"Books & Brunch Meetup"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"On bavarde","url":"https://www.meetup.com/north-york-french-language-meetup/events/316616449/","description":"RENCONTRE EN PRÉSENTIEL AU NORTH YORK CENTRE\n\nRejoignez-nous pour deux heures de conversation en français en personne.\n\nOÙ : North York Centre, Food Court\n(5150 rue Yonge, le batiment immediatement au nord du square Mel Lastman, métro North York)\n\nQUAND : samedi de 16h00 (4 pm) à 18h00\n\nA bientôt!","startDate":"2026-11-14T21:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-5-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"North York City Centre (same bldg as the NY Library), Food court","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"North York","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"5150 Yonge Street (WEST side!!!), next to Mel Lastman Sq., North York, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"North York French Language Meetup","url":"https://www.meetup.com/north-york-french-language-meetup/"},"performer":"North York French Language Meetup"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"VCF 9.1 Build & Deploy Hackathon","url":"https://www.meetup.com/vmware-vcf9-engineers-meetup-group/events/316364394/","description":"**VCF 9.1 Build & Deploy Hackathon**\nTeams design a customer environment, produce the architecture, validate prerequisites and work through a VCF deployment","startDate":"2026-11-15T00:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"","addressRegion":"","addressCountry":""}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"VMware VCF9 Engineers (Toronto/Ottawa) Group","url":"https://www.meetup.com/vmware-vcf9-engineers-meetup-group/"},"performer":"VMware VCF9 Engineers (Toronto/Ottawa) Group"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Meridian Arts Centre:  Canadian Golha Orchestra and Sepideh Raissadat","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-arts-and-culture/events/315296062/","description":"In this unforgettable concert, **the Canadian Golha Orchestra joins forces with acclaimed Persian music vocalist Sepideh Raissadat** to present rarely performed masterpieces of Iranian orchestral music. Timeless works by Rouhollah Khaleghi, Ali-Naqi Vaziri, Ali Tajvidi, and other pioneering composers will be brought to life through Raissadat’s velvety voice and the 40-piece orchestra’s expressive interpretation of these intricate and captivating melodies.\n\n***INFO Link here--***\n\nhttps://tolive.com/Event-Details-Page/reference/Canadian-Golha-Orchestra-2026?utm_medium=crosspromo&utm_source=partner&utm_campaign=canadiangolhaorchestra2026&utm_content=torontoisculture\n\nTicket link is below.\n\nInspired by the legacy of the *historic Golha radio orchestra*, the Canadian Golha Orchestra offers a refined interpretation of beloved repertoire by past masters, rooted in the Dastgāh tradition, alongside works by contemporary composers. Together, **the 40-piece orchestra** and Raissadat’s heartfelt artistry promise to immerse audiences in the profound beauty and emotional depth of Persian music.\n\n**More info here:**\n\nhttps://tolive.com/Event-Details-Page/reference/Canadian-Golha-Orchestra-2026\n\n**